					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-6938445#post-3913698</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-6938445/seven-days-with-mr-fish#post-3913698</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 16 Aug 2018 16:20:29 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Uncle Nicolini</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>3487700</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I fixed up the contradiction, thanks for pointing that out. :D</p> <p>As for your feelings on the article, I understand how you feel. I wrote Mr. Fish to be a passive character because my headcanon for him is that he doesn't really do anything, but things happen to him. My reason to write him as such is that he's such a normal guy (with a fish head) in a world full of things that are infinitely weirder than him. At least, this is how I interpreted him to be in the article. Because of that, it comes off as slice-of-life-ish with a twist of bizarre, which isn't for everyone so I totally understand how one wouldn't like it.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-6938445#post-3913671</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-6938445/seven-days-with-mr-fish#post-3913671</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 16 Aug 2018 16:03:25 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>SoullessSingularity</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>637830</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <blockquote> <p>Mr. Fish did not seem enthused, but it was hard to tell given his lack of facial range.</p> <p>&quot;Are you fucking serious right now?&quot; He questioned, his emotionless eyes glaring with furious vigor.</p> </blockquote> <p>I more or less downvoted here. The rest of the passage didn’t convince me to upvote. My main issue is that nothing really happens in this piece; there’s no sense of direction or story architecture, and not in a way that challenges the notion or story architecture either. It’s a series of events but not really a narrative. The thing I quoted above was just some part of the writing that rubbed me he wrong way, as it’s very contradictory.</p> <p>I’m the future I’d recommend looking broadly at some sort of stakes or conflict in the work that gives a character agency to move through it, thus giving the reader a feeling of direction. Otherwise the character is just responding to their environment, which makes your entire piece feel passive.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
